{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"kirnbergerIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, and A→E — are each narrowed by ¼ of the syntonic"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"comma, equal to ⁴√5 ≈ 696.578 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schisma (32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining seven","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one schisma equals one Pythagorean comma."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The four quarter-comma fifths make C–E a pure major third (5:4). Published in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Die Kunst des reinen Satzes in der Musik"}]},{"text":", Part II.","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament\/kirnbergerIII","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfac